    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60146" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κροταλ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>use rattles</i> or <i>castanets</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὲς τῶν γυναικῶν, κρόταλα ἔχουσαι,
					κροταλίζουσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.60
				</span></i>
			: hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵπποι κείν᾽ ὄχεα
				κροτάλιζον</span>
			<i>rattled</i> them <i>along</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.160
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later,
				<i>clap, applaud</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anaxil.
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.Chr.
				31.162
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				2.4
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				4.159e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.503f
			</span></i>.</div>
